  "rules": "Each player starts with {starting_coins} coins. Each player is secretly dealt a random ordering of the six prize values {prize_value_1}, {prize_value_2}, {prize_value_3}, {prize_value_4}, {prize_value_5} and {prize_value_6}, one value for each of auctions 1 to {auctions}. You see only your own list, so every player's six values total {prize_value_total}. Coin totals are public; prize values are private.\n\nThe game has {auctions} auctions. Each auction proceeds as follows.\n\n1. The auction number is announced.\n2. TALK: every player writes one short message at the same time without seeing the others. All messages are then shown to everyone. Messages are not binding: you may claim values, propose who takes which auction, or bluff.\n3. RAISE STAGES ({raise_stages} of them): at the same time, each player secretly chooses a raise, a whole number from 0 up to their available coins. Available coins are coins held minus everything already committed in this auction. Your committed bid for this auction is the sum of your raises so far. After each stage all committed bids are announced. A player with no available coins is not asked and raises 0.\n4. RESOLUTION: every player pays their full committed bid, which is subtracted from their coins, whether or not they win. If exactly one player has the highest committed bid and it is at least {min_winning_bid}, that player wins the prize and adds their OWN private value for this auction to their prize points; the value is not revealed to others. If two or more players tie for the highest bid, or all bids are 0, nobody wins the prize, and everyone still pays what they committed.\n5. The winner (or none) and everyone's remaining coins are announced. Committed bids reset to 0 for the next auction.\n\nEND: after auction {auctions}, each player's final score is coins remaining plus prize points. All private value lists are then revealed. The highest final score wins; players tied at the top share the win.",
